<title>USA: USDA attache-Argentine soy output at 13 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>USDA attache-Argentine soy output at 13 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. Agriculture Department attache pegged Argentina's 1996/97 soybean production at 13.0 million tonnes, below the official USDA forecast.</p>
<p>In the World Agricultural Supply and Demand report released Oct 11, USDA estimated Argentina soybean production at 13.50 million tonnes.</p>
<p>In a report released here Tuesday but dated Oct 1, the attache said his forecast was based on lower expected plantings of the normally higher yielding first crop soybeans due to greater area planted to wheat.</p>
<p>The attache also said planting delays may reduce yield potential as farmers wait for adequate rainfall in some regions.</p>
</text>
